//   and this file's BaseMotionMethod enum is the back-filled result.
//
// Semantic boundaries (NRCP §17.2; read the original):
//   - SetVelocity is a **short-lived velocity target layer** in the body frame, not a high-level intent of
//     "get ready and start moving by yourself"; it **doesn't implicitly perform** long posture changes such as standing up.
//   - Standing / getting up / sitting down belong to a separate Posture interface/Operation (not this interface).
//   - Differential-drive vehicles may not support linear_y, but must report it explicitly in MotionState.supports_linear_y.
//   - When a legged Provider's preconditions aren't met (sitting / mid posture change) it returns FAILED_PRECONDITION +
//     BaseMotionReason.LOCOMOTION_NOT_READY, and must not cram a slow stand-up into SetVelocity.
//   - Stop() is an ordinary controlled stop and **doesn't replace** SafetyHalt (SafetyHalt isn't controlled by App Permissions
//     and isn't in this interface).
//
// Units and frames: linear = m/s, angular = rad/s, both in the **body frame**.
//   linear_x positive towards the body's front; linear_y positive towards the body's left; angular_z positive counter-clockwise.
